482	/// Remaps ranges.
483	///
484	/// Useful in combination with
485	/// [`SyntaxNode::synthesize_mapped`](super::SyntaxNode::synthesize_mapped) to
486	/// have accurate error spans for source text that is non-consecutive in its
487	/// source file (for instance, Typst code in a doc comment with start-of-line
